<Placemark>   <name>Alby Mesolithic Village</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <b>County/Region:</b> Öland <b>Alt Name:</b> Alby, Alby People <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>4</b> Condition: <b>2</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>3</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 56.49023 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 16.57378<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Scandinavia/Sweden/thumb/aalbymesolithiclagoon.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Mesolithic settlers in Alby on the island of Öland in Sweden built some of the earliest recognisable villages in Northern Europe. The earliest of these peoples likely traversed the Kalmar Strait via ...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=18116" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#2_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>16.57378,56.49023,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Buttle 266</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <b>County/Region:</b> Gotland <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>5</b>  Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>4</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 57.39538 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 18.50227<br />
                    Ancient Village or Settlement in Gotland. A housing plot of approximately 15 x 6 m, as well as at least one not fully defined housing plot and probably leftovers of outdoor activities, for example, an...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=51552" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#2_g</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>18.50227,57.39538,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Kanaljorden</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <b>County/Region:</b> Östergötland <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>2</b> Condition: <b>1</b> (5 is best)   (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 58.533513 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 15.04824<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Scandinavia/Sweden/thumb/Kanaljorden-lyft.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Recent archaeological excavations at the site of Kanaljorden in the town of Motala, Östergötland in Central Sweden have unearthed a complex Mesolithic site with ceremonial depositions of human crani...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=30542" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#2_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>15.04824,58.533513,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Kaunisvaara Settlements</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <b>County/Region:</b> Norrbotten <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>1</b> Condition: <b>Destroyed</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 67.38328 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 23.33557<br />
                    Ancient Settlement in Norrbotten. An important new find by a team of Swedish archaeologists indicates that the Finland-Sweden border area around the Torne River Valley was inhabited up to 11,000 years...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=24418" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#2_y</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>23.33557,67.38328,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Lejsturojr Settlement</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <b>County/Region:</b> Gotland <b>Alt Name:</b> Rone 70:3 <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>5</b> Condition: <b>2</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>3</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 57.18766 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 18.47674<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Scandinavia/Sweden/thumb/Lesturojr_settlement__0752_.JPG" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Ancient Village or Settlement in Gotland. Lejsturojr Settlement is an Iron Age cluster of farm buildings a short detour from the main track to the massive Lejsturojr stone cairn.  Not much of the site...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=30239" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#2_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>18.47674,57.18766,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Lillberget</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <b>County/Region:</b> Norrbotten <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>4</b> Condition: <b>1</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>5</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 66.405444 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 22.66784<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Scandinavia/Sweden/thumb/vjw_IMG_2824.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Grave and settlement area, partially surveyed, approx. 180 x 120 m (NW-SE). Consisting of 6 oval settlement ditch, 2 irregularly rounded settlement ditches, 1 red ochre deposit, 1 flatland grave and 1...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=55655" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#2_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>22.66784,66.405444,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Rosendal</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <b>County/Region:</b> Öland <b>Alt Name:</b> RAÄ Böda 68:1 <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>5</b> Condition: <b>5</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>5</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 57.27335 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 17.01315<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Scandinavia/Sweden/thumb/rosendal001.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Iron Age settlement and cemetery in Öland. Remains of an Iron Age settlement - in the western wood of the site there are three standing stones and cairns (57.27424N,17.00910E), which could be a cemet...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=45703" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#2_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>17.01315,57.27335,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Skateholm Mesolithic Settlement</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <b>County/Region:</b> Skåne <b>Alt Name:</b> Skateholm I, Skateholm II <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>3</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 55.379167 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 13.470833<br />
                    Skateholm settlement is a settlement with associated burial ground from the Mesolithic period, the graves have been dated from about 5250 to 4900 BC. About 90 graves have been found and investigated i...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=32658" >Link To More Information</a><br />
